{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03SB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-vanishing-affine-curves}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-vanishing-torsion-coefficients}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29902d66f95a47b9586710cf1b67c08cd504353dedfad08fa8016a236906e29e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe goal of this section is to prove the basic finiteness and vanishing\nresults for cohomology of torsion sheaves on curves, see\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\nIn Section <REF_0002>\nwe will discuss constructible sheaves of torsion modules\nover a Noetherian ring.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:245221b703115d4bc2d70b9f45ce624b1c8de7dec2cf7dc912353cb340b78d88", "unit_id": "tag:03SB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "situation", "parent_tag": "03SB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\leq 1$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$X_\\etale$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{situation}\n\\label{situation-what-to-prove}\n", "suffix": "\\end{situation}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:59afffc2eb4baaa38689ec28726e7fb57f0cf5ebff56a78cfa81eef246194f52", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5e36031d60f25a51f334f7251eee8019e20d2ff8ec3596d5257f2e4129dbc6a1", "source_text": "Here <MATH_0001> is an algebraically closed field, <MATH_0002> is a separated, finite type\nscheme of dimension <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004>, and <MATH_0005> is a torsion\nabelian sheaf on <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70c0263fa81b565c0cecc54d0df836fb480b525c46bbfaba1222b1d32b7d634f", "unit_id": "tag:0A52:statement"}
